  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Hydrogen is the first element in the periodic table&nbsp;and has the atomic number one. Those elements which have the same atomic number but a different mass number are called isotopes. There are three isotopes of hydrogen namely, protium <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mprescripts/><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></mmultiscripts></math>, deuterium <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mprescripts/><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mmultiscripts></math>&nbsp;or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>&nbsp;and lastly tritium <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mprescripts/><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mmultiscripts></math>&nbsp;or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. The isotopes are different because of the different number of neutrons present in them.</p><p>Isotopes of Hydrogen:<br /><br /><img height=\"70\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/40494040-53e7-4042-9313-3569e348a860-image.png\" width=\"243\" /><br /><br />Among all three isotopes only Tritium is radioactive.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
